course: dictionary
lesson: 11283
title: Writing: one word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: One word can have several meanings, and the sentence around it tells you which one you need. Writing can mean the activity of putting words on paper, the words themselves, someone's handwriting, or a book or story someone has written.
explain: «There was writing on the wall.» Here writing means words that are written. Ask yourself: which meaning fits this sentence? Then try it in place of the word to check.
explain: «I can't read your writing.» Here the clue is «read»: writing means handwriting, the way a person writes their letters.
explain: Some phrases have set meanings. «Please put your request in writing» means written down, so it is official. «The writing is on the wall» means trouble is clearly coming. It does not mean there are real words on a wall.
fact: Writing means putting words on paper or a screen.
fact: «Writings» in the plural means the books, stories or poems that someone has written.
fact: In school, writing is a subject, where teachers mark your ideas, spelling, punctuation and handwriting.
fact: Writing was invented separately in Mesopotamia about 5,200 years ago, and in China over 3,000 years ago.
fact: «In writing» means written down, and «the writing is on the wall» means trouble is coming.
exercise: In «There was writing on the wall.», what does writing mean? | The job of being a writer | The activity of drawing pictures | Books in a library | *Words that are written
exercise: Mum says, «I can't read your writing.» What does writing mean here? | The job of being a writer | A book someone has written | *A person's handwriting | Pictures drawn in colour
exercise: Miss Patel says, «Please put your request in writing.» What does in writing mean? | It means drawn in pictures | It means done in a hurry | *It means written down, so it is official | It means shouted out loud
test: Which meaning of writing fits «Her writings are read in schools all over the world.»? | The job of being a teacher | *Books, stories or poems that someone has written | Neat handwriting | The activity of putting words on paper
test: In «My favourite lesson is creative writing», what does writing mean? | Words on a wall | Official papers signed in ink | A person's handwriting | *A school subject where you write your own stories and poems
exam: What does the phrase «the writing is on the wall» mean? | Someone has painted a picture on a wall | Everything is fine and safe | There is a new wall to paint | *Trouble is clearly coming
